    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d534">

                <pb facs="1003" n="981" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg981"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Secretary’s Memoranda, Lot 53 D 444</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1950-08-28">August 28, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum of Conversation With the President</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Item No. 4 <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador to Israel</hi>
                </p>
                <p>I explained to the President the reasons why we thought it would be most unwise
                    to appoint General Riley as Ambassador to Israel. He said that I need not argue
                    with him. He was totally convinced that we were right. General Riley’s present
                    task was of the most vital importance and should not be prejudiced in any
                    way.</p>
                <p>He would like to have us canvass the field, both inside and outside the
                    Department and would like to appoint a very level-headed man. This person should
                    not be a partisan. He should be concerned with the interests of the United
                    States. While he should be sympathetic with the nation to which he was
                    accredited, he should not cause antagonism to the Arabs.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
